WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.260
To understand what real numbers are,

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.300
all you need to understand is the number line.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.660
Positive numbers to the right of Zero.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.140
And negative numbers to the left of Zero.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.220
You will hear various complicated definitions of real numbers

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.680
but here's the simplest one.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.660
Any number, that can be plotted on a number line is called a real number.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.060
Let's look at a few examples.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.060
Say 'minus 2.'

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.760
Yes, it can be plotted on the number line. It's this point.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.300
So minus two is a real number.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.000
What about zero point five?

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.880
Even though it's not an integer, it can be plotted on the number line.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.720
It will be somewhere here.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.040
Now let's look at another number.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.540
Root two.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.560
Which is also called as square root of two.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.200
If we calculate the value of root two,

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.540
we get it as 1.414 approximately.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.920
The digits after the decimal point do not end.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.120
These kind of numbers are called non-terminating decimal numbers.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.300
And yes, these numbers too can be plotted on the number line.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.740
Plotting a non-terminating number might sound weird,

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.700
but yes, it's possible.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.920
So 'root two' is also a real number.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.300
And what about the special number Pi?

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:29.380
it approximately equals 3.14159.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.000
Pi is also a non-terminating decimal number.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.000
And yes, it can be plotted on the number line,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.220
which makes it a real number.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.400
So that's our definition.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.400
Any number that can be plotted on a number line is called a real number.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:49.620
Now let's talk a bit about the different kinds of numbers we know.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:53.240
The first kind is numbers with terminating decimals.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.700
Numbers like 0.375.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.680
The number stops at a point and does not go on and on.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.520
Then we have non-terminating recurring decimals.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:08.920
Numbers like 0.6666 and so on.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.120
The sixes don't end.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:14.560
It's called recurring since the same number reoccurs

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.920
and non-terminating since it reoccurs infinitely.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.760
And the third type is non-terminating non-recurring decimals.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.960
We just saw an example of this type.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:31.260
Root two. It approximately equals 1.4142.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.420
And the digits after the decimal do not end.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.880
Hence, it's called non-terminating. It's called non-recurring ,

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.080
since there is no specific pattern of re-occurrence.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.100
Broadly, these are the three types of numbers we see in Mathematics.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:53.260
'Terminating', 'non-terminating recurring'and 'non-terminating non-recurring'.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.040
These two categories together are called Rational numbers.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:01.560
and the numbers in this category are called Irrational numbers.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.380
These two categories together form Real numbers.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.600
This is the other definition of Real numbers.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:14.180
Rational numbers and Irrational numbers together form Real numbers.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.280
In the second part of this video,

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:20.680
we will look at all categories real numbers comprise off.

